1
00:01:22,632 --> 00:01:25,174
They are an army unlike any other...

2
00:01:25,257 --> 00:01:29,092
crusading across the stars
toward a place called UnderVerse,

3
00:01:29,176 --> 00:01:31,093
their promised land...

4
00:01:31,177 --> 00:01:34,470
a constellation of dark new worlds.

5
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:36,970
Necromongers, they're called.

6
00:01:37,054 --> 00:01:41,429
And if they cannot convert you,
they will kill you.

7
00:01:43,014 --> 00:01:46,097
Leading them, the Lord Marshal.

8
00:01:46,181 --> 00:01:50,226
He alone has made a pilgrimage
to the gates of the UnderVerse...

9
00:01:50,309 --> 00:01:53,518
and returned a different being.

10
00:01:53,601 --> 00:01:56,852
Stronger. Stranger.

11
00:01:56,936 --> 00:02:00,230
Half alive and half...

12
00:02:00,313 --> 00:02:03,064
something else.

13
00:02:13,651 --> 00:02:17,653
If we are to survive,
a new balance must be found.

14
00:02:18,735 --> 00:02:21,694
In normal times,
evil would be fought by good.

15
00:02:21,736 --> 00:02:24,738
But in times like these, well,

16
00:02:24,821 --> 00:02:27,988
it should be fought
by another kind of evil.

17
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:06,379
Linin' him up for you.
Port-side shot comin' up.
Steady. Here we go.

18
00:03:13,631 --> 00:03:16,424
Steady.

19
00:03:16,466 --> 00:03:19,508
Take it. Take it!

20
00:03:19,591 --> 00:03:22,008
Take the shot!

21
00:03:24,134 --> 00:03:26,761
Shit!
Toombs, we're runnin' out of road!

22
00:03:26,844 --> 00:03:29,011
Shut up! I got it! Again!

23
00:03:31,553 --> 00:03:34,388
Now!

24
00:03:34,429 --> 00:03:36,555
Toombs!

25
00:03:50,812 --> 00:03:54,270
Riddick.

26
00:03:55,689 --> 00:03:58,398
I don't know, Toombs.
Looks kinda tight.

27
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:02,108
Not where I'm sittin'.
This is the biggest payday ever,

28
00:04:02,191 --> 00:04:05,234
So throw on a fresh pair of panties.
Let's get this right.

29
00:04:15,695 --> 00:04:20,072
Three meters clearance port-side.
One and a half meters starboard.

30
00:04:20,155 --> 00:04:22,615
We got a choke point comin' up.

31
00:04:35,161 --> 00:04:37,704
What the shit was that?

32
00:04:39,538 --> 00:04:42,664
Tags, you got eyes on Riddick?

33
00:04:42,747 --> 00:04:45,539
Tags?

34
00:04:49,124 --> 00:04:51,583
Jesus.

35
00:04:51,667 --> 00:04:54,626
He just ghosted two guys,
and I never even saw him.

36
00:04:56,293 --> 00:05:00,211
What do you think, Toombs?
I mean, maybe we oughta just...
I think you're my new gunner.

37
00:05:00,294 --> 00:05:02,295
Grab a Gat.

38
00:05:09,798 --> 00:05:11,883
Stay on top of him this time.

39
00:05:39,767 --> 00:05:43,437
You made three mistakes.

40
00:05:44,936 --> 00:05:48,480
First, you took the job.

41
00:05:48,564 --> 00:05:50,605
Second, you came light.

42
00:05:50,647 --> 00:05:55,274
A four-man crew for me?
Fuckin' insulting.

43
00:05:55,315 --> 00:05:58,484
But the worst mistake you made...

44
00:06:00,358 --> 00:06:02,484
Empty gun rack.

45
00:06:07,278 --> 00:06:10,237
- What's the bounty on my head?
- One mil.

46
00:06:12,989 --> 00:06:17,615
- One-point-five.
- What slam pays 1.5 for a convict?

47
00:06:17,699 --> 00:06:19,949
Private party.

48
00:06:20,032 --> 00:06:22,993
Hey, hey, hey, hey!
Guy, guy! Easy! Anonymous.

49
00:06:23,034 --> 00:06:26,410
- That's what the sheet said.
- What planet?

50
00:06:27,786 --> 00:06:29,744
Helion Prime.

51
00:06:37,038 --> 00:06:39,956
Whoa. Where you goin'?
Last question.

52
00:06:40,039 --> 00:06:43,708
And you better get this one right, merc.

53
00:06:43,749 --> 00:06:45,666
Whose ship is this?

54
00:06:45,749 --> 00:06:48,418
Mine?

55
00:07:08,551 --> 00:07:11,051
Knew they'd come for me.

56
00:07:11,093 --> 00:07:14,094
Took 'em five years, but I knew.

57
00:07:14,177 --> 00:07:18,846
You don't expect these mercs
to have any honor, any code.

58
00:07:20,637 --> 00:07:24,973
But this new bounty from a holy man,

59
00:07:25,056 --> 00:07:28,016
a guy whose neck I saved...

60
00:07:29,516 --> 00:07:31,434
Well, lesson learned.

61
00:07:31,517 --> 00:07:34,227
No such word as "friend."

62
00:07:34,311 --> 00:07:37,519
Can only end bad
when you let someone get too close.

63
00:07:38,729 --> 00:07:40,937
Bad for them.

64
00:07:43,689 --> 00:07:49,064
So now it's back to all the brightness...
and everything I hate.

65
00:07:50,107 --> 00:07:52,941
Wonder if she'll be there.

66
00:08:02,778 --> 00:08:07,780
Act like an animal and
I'm gonna slot you up like one.
This one is always in trouble.

67
00:08:07,864 --> 00:08:09,823
I knew it!
I smell it.

68
00:08:30,872 --> 00:08:32,581
Get in there!

69
00:08:58,341 --> 00:09:00,342
Can we shut the goddamn noise?

70
00:09:32,770 --> 00:09:36,689
They say most of your brain
shuts down in cryosleep.

71
00:09:36,731 --> 00:09:40,272
Brain shuts down in cryosleep.

72
00:09:40,355 --> 00:09:43,523
- All but the primitive side.
- All but the primitive side.

73
00:09:43,607 --> 00:09:45,900
The animal side.

74
00:09:45,983 --> 00:09:49,525
All but the Furyan side.

75
00:09:54,235 --> 00:09:58,988
Some of us still remember
the true crime that happened
here on Furya.

76
00:10:01,822 --> 00:10:04,490
And once you wake...

77
00:10:04,573 --> 00:10:07,325
truly wake...

78
00:10:09,742 --> 00:10:11,993
you'll remember too.

79
00:10:16,535 --> 00:10:20,287
Helion Prime is on alert condition four.

80
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:30,124
Unrecognized craft.
You need to follow me to Spaceport Six
for security inspections.

81
00:10:30,208 --> 00:10:33,458
Hey! Do you hear me?

82
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:36,168
Follow me to Spaceport Six now!

83
00:11:25,770 --> 00:11:27,800
Imam, pray for us.

84
00:11:27,447 --> 00:11:30,739
It was confirmed
two seasons back. Yes.

85
00:11:30,780 --> 00:11:33,114
They're coming here.
I mean, are we next?

86
00:11:33,197 --> 00:11:35,198
Militants storm...

87
00:11:35,282 --> 00:11:38,408
Yes. But going to the underground
shelters if it happens...

88
00:11:38,490 --> 00:11:40,659
You're right.
That's what I thought too.

89
00:11:41,243 --> 00:11:43,702
Are you staying or leaving?

90
00:11:44,285 --> 00:11:46,619
It's the end of everything.
Everything!

91
00:11:46,703 --> 00:11:50,162
Well, my neighbors...
Half my street is gone.

92
00:11:50,245 --> 00:11:52,163
What are we gonna do?
I don't know. I don't know.

93
00:11:52,204 --> 00:11:54,165
Hood of the devil.
That's what someone called 'em.

94
00:11:54,205 --> 00:11:56,331
Them? Who is them?
Some kind of new creature...

95
00:11:56,415 --> 00:11:58,374
This is nonsense.
It's all nonsense.

96
00:11:59,458 --> 00:12:02,375
So tall that it touches the clouds.

97
00:12:02,417 --> 00:12:06,792
And there's nothing around
this statue, this colossus.
Nothing left.

98
00:12:06,876 --> 00:12:09,127
It's their calling card.

99
00:12:19,590 --> 00:12:22,799
Did you know all your doors were locked?

100
00:12:28,385 --> 00:12:30,218
Five years ago,

101
00:12:30,302 --> 00:12:32,800
I took two people off that planet...

102
00:12:32,810 --> 00:12:37,513
A kid, Jack,
who everyone else thought was a boy,:

103
00:12:37,597 --> 00:12:40,264
and a holy man...

104
00:12:40,347 --> 00:12:42,307
searching for New Mecca.

105
00:12:46,348 --> 00:12:48,433
Your wife...

106
00:12:50,051 --> 00:12:52,009
She's in the shower.

107
00:12:53,093 --> 00:12:57,053
I told one man...

108
00:12:57,136 --> 00:13:00,305
where I might go.

109
00:13:00,389 --> 00:13:04,306
I showed trust to one man.

110
00:13:04,390 --> 00:13:07,891
Did I make a mistake, Imam?

111
00:13:07,975 --> 00:13:10,309
There is no simple answer.

112
00:13:10,351 --> 00:13:15,061
Whatever was said
was meant to give us a chance...

113
00:13:15,144 --> 00:13:17,144
a fighting chance.

114
00:13:17,561 --> 00:13:20,600
Were it not for the threat of invasion,
I never would have betrayed you.

115
00:13:20,610 --> 00:13:24,188
I give you my word, Riddick.
Riddick!

116
00:13:26,730 --> 00:13:28,689
Riddick!

117
00:13:30,607 --> 00:13:33,150
And a daughter...

118
00:13:35,109 --> 00:13:38,193
- No!
- whose name would be...

119
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:40,820
If you have issue with me,
you let it be with me.

120
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:43,362
You need not know their names.
Ziza.

121
00:13:45,613 --> 00:13:47,530
My name is Ziza.

122
00:13:48,823 --> 00:13:50,740
Ziza.

123
00:13:52,448 --> 00:13:56,450
- Cute kid.
- Did you really kill monsters?

124
00:13:56,534 --> 00:13:59,034
The ones that were gonna
hurt my father?

125
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:03,035
Such are our bedtime stories.

126
00:14:03,119 --> 00:14:05,787
Go, Ziza. Go on!

127
00:14:10,831 --> 00:14:14,957
So now who do I have to kill
to get this payday off my head?

128
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:35,423
It is said the comet
always precedes them...

129
00:14:35,464 --> 00:14:37,965
these world-enders.

130
00:14:40,049 --> 00:14:41,967
The Coalsack planets are gone.

131
00:14:42,050 --> 00:14:44,884
Eight million settlers missing.

132
00:14:44,968 --> 00:14:48,593
The entire Aquilan System is gone too.

133
00:14:48,677 --> 00:14:53,054
Helion Prime shares its sunlight
with all worlds nearby.

134
00:14:55,222 --> 00:14:59,890
If we fall, they fall.

135
00:14:59,974 --> 00:15:02,308
And after that...

136
00:15:02,392 --> 00:15:05,560
My God,
how do I save my family?

137
00:15:09,936 --> 00:15:12,727
Have you heard anything I've said?

138
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:18,646
You said
it's all circling the drain...
the whole universe.

139
00:15:18,729 --> 00:15:20,689
Right?
That's right.

140
00:15:29,693 --> 00:15:31,861
Had to end sometime.

141
00:15:49,449 --> 00:15:51,450
The one you want is now here.

142
00:16:09,416 --> 00:16:11,834
And whose throat is this?

143
00:16:12,834 --> 00:16:17,502
If you cut my throat, I'll not be able to
rescind the offer that brought you here.

144
00:16:17,586 --> 00:16:20,128
Nor tell you why it's so vital
that you did come.

145
00:16:20,169 --> 00:16:23,088
The blade comes off
when the bounty comes off.

146
00:16:23,171 --> 00:16:26,796
This is Aereon,
an envoy from the Elemental race.

147
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:29,213
She means you no harm.

148
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:36,800
There are very few of us
who have met a Necromonger
and lived to speak of it.

149
00:16:36,884 --> 00:16:41,510
So when I choose to speak of it,
you should choose to listen.

150
00:16:41,594 --> 00:16:43,637
Necromonger.

151
00:16:43,721 --> 00:16:49,014
It is the name that will convert
or kill every last human life...

152
00:16:49,096 --> 00:16:52,181
unless the universe
can rebalance itself.

153
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:58,518
Maybe you should pretend like you're talkin'
to someone educated in the penal system.

154
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:01,767
In fact, don't pretend.

155
00:17:01,851 --> 00:17:05,227
Balance is everything
to elementals.

156
00:17:05,269 --> 00:17:07,270
Water to fire.
Earth to air.

157
00:17:07,353 --> 00:17:09,687
We have 33 different words for it.

158
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:13,500
But now we have only time
to speak of the balance of opposites.

159
00:17:13,639 --> 00:17:17,516
There is a story, Riddick,
of young male Furyans...

160
00:17:17,557 --> 00:17:20,099
strangled at birth...

161
00:17:20,183 --> 00:17:22,352
strangled with their own cords.

162
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:26,728
When Aereon told this story
to the Helion leaders,

163
00:17:27,012 --> 00:17:29,095
I told her of you.

164
00:17:29,178 --> 00:17:32,264
- What do you know of your early years?
- Do you remember your home world?

165
00:17:32,347 --> 00:17:34,806
- Where it was?
- Have you met any others?

166
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:36,890
Others like yourself.

167
00:17:39,515 --> 00:17:43,559
Sister, they don't know
what to do with just one of me.

168
00:17:43,442 --> 00:17:45,943
Open up in there!

169
00:17:46,826 --> 00:17:48,800
- Stand back!
- Open up!

170
00:17:48,810 --> 00:17:50,702
They are searching houses!
Shh!

171
00:17:50,786 --> 00:17:53,788
They look for a man
who came here today.
They think he might be a spy.

172
00:17:53,871 --> 00:17:56,163
A spy?
Did someone see him
come here today?

173
00:17:56,247 --> 00:17:57,914
Did they?
Lajjun, stop!

174
00:17:57,997 --> 00:18:02,541
We're sure he's in there!
I will send them away.
But wait one minute, please.

175
00:18:02,624 --> 00:18:05,792
Will you wait one minute
to save worlds?

176
00:18:07,501 --> 00:18:10,252
Not my fight.

177
00:18:10,293 --> 00:18:12,586
So, you will leave us
to our fate,

178
00:18:12,628 --> 00:18:14,961
just like you did her.

179
00:18:15,044 --> 00:18:18,296
Break it down!

180
00:18:20,046 --> 00:18:21,130
Get him!

181
00:18:21,172 --> 00:18:23,507
Come. Let us try to send them away.

182
00:18:27,007 --> 00:18:29,217
Move it. Come on.
Leave us alone!

183
00:18:31,467 --> 00:18:34,886
There is no one here!

184
00:18:34,928 --> 00:18:38,720
You don't understand.
He can help us! He can help us!

185
00:18:41,930 --> 00:18:43,931
Go!

186
00:18:49,308 --> 00:18:52,267
You're not afraid of the dark, are you?

187
00:19:12,650 --> 00:19:15,235
- Get him!
- Where is he?

188
00:19:15,277 --> 00:19:17,610
In there!

189
00:19:44,620 --> 00:19:47,079
You mentioned her.

190
00:19:47,162 --> 00:19:50,038
She, uh...

191
00:19:50,122 --> 00:19:52,039
She went looking for you.

192
00:19:52,123 --> 00:19:55,499
People died.
She went to prison.

193
00:19:55,582 --> 00:19:59,418
I... I don't remember where.

194
00:20:00,418 --> 00:20:05,877
But it was a world so hot
you not survive on the surface.

195
00:20:05,919 --> 00:20:09,421
Crematoria.
Young Jack.

196
00:20:09,503 --> 00:20:11,713
She thought of you
as her older brother.

197
00:20:11,754 --> 00:20:14,797
She worshipped you.
You were supposed to watch her.

198
00:20:15,965 --> 00:20:18,590
She never forgave you...

199
00:20:18,674 --> 00:20:22,049
for leaving just when
she needed you most.

200
00:20:22,133 --> 00:20:27,218
She needed to
stay away from me.
You all do.

201
00:20:29,511 --> 00:20:31,970
Riddick.

202
00:20:33,722 --> 00:20:37,097
Are you gonna stop
the new monsters now?

203
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:53,853
Furyans.
Defiant to the end.

204
00:21:31,659 --> 00:21:33,576
No, no.

205
00:21:33,659 --> 00:21:36,161
We go to the shelter.

206
00:21:36,202 --> 00:21:38,703
We take only ourselves.

207
00:21:59,836 --> 00:22:01,837
Stay close.

208
00:22:34,347 --> 00:22:36,932
No!

209
00:23:48,125 --> 00:23:50,751
Flight leaders, get all squads
off the ground now.

210
00:23:50,834 --> 00:23:53,669
We have heavy inbound.

211
00:23:54,795 --> 00:23:56,921
Follow me in!

212
00:24:15,136 --> 00:24:17,303
The next shelter.
This way!

213
00:24:17,386 --> 00:24:19,388
Yeah!

214
00:24:19,472 --> 00:24:21,847
Whoo-hoo!

215
00:24:42,896 --> 00:24:46,105
I'll see if it's safe.

216
00:24:51,316 --> 00:24:54,859
- Stay back!
- Come, Ziza.

217
00:25:12,698 --> 00:25:15,033
Come!

218
00:25:34,540 --> 00:25:36,581
You following me?

219
00:26:14,137 --> 00:26:16,180
Lajjun and Ziza!

220
00:26:16,263 --> 00:26:18,972
When it's over.
Let me go.
I must get to my family!

221
00:26:19,056 --> 00:26:21,390
When it's over.

222
00:26:47,733 --> 00:26:49,900
I borrowed a ship.

223
00:26:49,983 --> 00:26:53,568
You can ride along,
if you don't mind riding with a convict.

224
00:26:53,652 --> 00:26:56,986
I thank you, but I must get
my family across the river.

225
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:59,320
God willing, there is still
a shelter I can get them...

226
00:26:59,403 --> 00:27:01,405
I'm sure God has his tricks,

227
00:27:01,489 --> 00:27:05,281
but getting out of places
no one else can,

228
00:27:05,323 --> 00:27:07,533
that's one of mine.

229
00:27:08,533 --> 00:27:10,617
Let's get your family.

230
00:27:13,201 --> 00:27:15,202
Aah!

231
00:27:44,754 --> 00:27:46,755
In here.

232
00:27:47,881 --> 00:27:50,257
Get in.

233
00:27:51,966 --> 00:27:54,174
Shh.

234
00:28:58,407 --> 00:29:00,991
- Imam!
- Don't follow me.

235
00:30:35,734 --> 00:30:38,568
There will be
an afterlife for me.

236
00:30:40,235 --> 00:30:42,153
Will there be for you?

237
00:32:00,140 --> 00:32:03,682
Let's go replenish the ranks.

238
00:32:16,521 --> 00:32:18,980
Never fails to inspire, does it?

239
00:32:19,022 --> 00:32:21,272
Each time a dynasty falls.

240
00:32:21,355 --> 00:32:24,857
Remember your place,
Dame Vaako.

241
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:27,765
My place is at your side,
dear husband.

242
00:32:27,849 --> 00:32:29,976
From here till UnderVerse come.

243
00:32:54,402 --> 00:32:57,694
In this 'verse,

244
00:32:57,736 --> 00:33:01,821
life is antagonistic
to the natural state.

245
00:33:03,362 --> 00:33:08,406
Here, humans in all
their various races...

246
00:33:08,489 --> 00:33:11,617
are a spontaneous outbreak...

247
00:33:11,700 --> 00:33:13,908
an unguided mistake.

248
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:15,951
Our purpose...

249
00:33:16,035 --> 00:33:19,869
is to correct that mistake.

250
00:33:21,078 --> 00:33:24,370
Because there is another 'verse...

251
00:33:24,454 --> 00:33:29,456
a 'verse where life
is welcomed and cherished.

252
00:33:29,539 --> 00:33:35,333
A ravishing, ever-new place
called UnderVerse.

253
00:33:36,583 --> 00:33:40,251
But the road to that 'verse...

254
00:33:40,335 --> 00:33:42,336
crosses over the threshold.

255
00:33:42,419 --> 00:33:45,503
Threshold!
Take us to the threshold!

256
00:33:45,587 --> 00:33:49,379
What you call... death.

257
00:33:49,463 --> 00:33:55,257
So it is this 'verse
that must be cleansed of life,

258
00:33:55,341 --> 00:33:59,592
so that UnderVerse
can populate and prosper.

259
00:34:02,177 --> 00:34:06,720
Look around you.
Every Necromonger in this hall,

260
00:34:06,803 --> 00:34:11,262
every one of the Legion Vast that just
swept aside your defenses in one night...

261
00:34:11,346 --> 00:34:14,096
was once like you.

262
00:34:14,138 --> 00:34:16,890
Fought as feebly as you.

263
00:34:17,974 --> 00:34:20,891
Every Necromonger
that lives today...

264
00:34:20,974 --> 00:34:23,100
is a convert.

265
00:34:23,184 --> 00:34:28,353
- There'll be no conversions!
- We all began as something else!

266
00:34:30,644 --> 00:34:35,105
It was hard for me to accept, too,
when I first heard these words.

267
00:34:35,147 --> 00:34:37,731
But I changed.

268
00:34:37,814 --> 00:34:40,149
I let them take away my pain.

269
00:34:40,231 --> 00:34:44,442
- You betrayed your faith!
- Just as you will change...

270
00:34:44,484 --> 00:34:49,943
when you realize that the threshold
to the UnderVerse will be crossed...

271
00:34:50,026 --> 00:34:54,196
only by those who have
embraced the Necromonger faith.

272
00:34:54,279 --> 00:34:57,404
For those of you
who will right now...

273
00:34:57,488 --> 00:35:01,531
drop to your knees
and ask to be purified.

274
00:35:01,615 --> 00:35:05,157
We will not renounce our faith!
No one here
will do what you ask.

275
00:35:06,575 --> 00:35:08,034
It is unthinkable!

276
00:35:08,117 --> 00:35:13,453
This is a world of many peoples,
many religions!

277
00:35:13,536 --> 00:35:17,954
And we simply cannot
and will not be converted!

278
00:35:17,996 --> 00:35:20,789
Then I'll take your soul.

279
00:35:32,167 --> 00:35:34,710
Join him...

280
00:35:34,794 --> 00:35:38,003
or join me.

281
00:35:57,928 --> 00:36:00,595
This is your one chance.

282
00:36:00,678 --> 00:36:03,137
Take the Lord Marshal's offer
and bow.

283
00:36:03,221 --> 00:36:06,054
I bow to no man.

284
00:36:13,225 --> 00:36:15,226
He's not a man.

285
00:36:15,309 --> 00:36:18,976
He's the holy Half-Dead
who has seen the UnderVerse.

286
00:36:19,060 --> 00:36:21,560
Look, I'm not
with everyone here.

287
00:36:21,644 --> 00:36:24,229
But I will take a piece of him.

288
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:32,815
A piece you will have.

289
00:37:00,825 --> 00:37:02,825
Stop him!

290
00:37:15,288 --> 00:37:17,705
Irgun. One of my best.

291
00:37:17,789 --> 00:37:20,249
If you say so.

292
00:37:23,959 --> 00:37:26,210
What do you think of this blade?

293
00:37:35,964 --> 00:37:38,339
I think it's a half-gram heavy
on the back end.

294
00:37:38,422 --> 00:37:40,382
In our faith,

295
00:37:40,423 --> 00:37:42,590
you keep what you kill.

296
00:37:49,885 --> 00:37:51,927
Are you familiar to me?

297
00:37:54,803 --> 00:37:58,304
Have we met
on some distant field?

298
00:37:59,471 --> 00:38:01,181
You'd think I'd remember.

299
00:38:02,722 --> 00:38:06,016
You'd think I would too.

300
00:38:06,058 --> 00:38:09,642
Take him before the Quasi-Deads.

301
00:38:16,603 --> 00:38:19,980
Perhaps the breeder
would do it...

302
00:38:20,063 --> 00:38:22,564
if somebody just asked him.

303
00:38:24,523 --> 00:38:26,941
It is a rare offer.

304
00:38:28,856 --> 00:38:31,817
A visit inside Necropolis.

305
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:37,111
It's been a long time
since I smelled beautiful.

306
00:38:38,902 --> 00:38:41,028
Let me show you the way.

307
00:39:34,265 --> 00:39:36,557
Beautiful eyes.

308
00:39:36,641 --> 00:39:38,642
Come.

309
00:39:41,392 --> 00:39:45,476
The last six Lord Marshals
have called this home.

310
00:39:45,559 --> 00:39:47,810
Magnificent, isn't it?

311
00:39:47,894 --> 00:39:51,646
I might have gone
a different way.
True of us all.

312
00:39:53,688 --> 00:39:57,773
Converts receiving the mark
of the Necromonger.

313
00:40:00,023 --> 00:40:03,275
They learn how one pain
can lessen another.

314
00:40:17,405 --> 00:40:19,407
There now.

315
00:40:21,073 --> 00:40:24,367
That is just... perfect.

316
00:40:27,742 --> 00:40:30,952
The more you resist them,

317
00:40:31,035 --> 00:40:33,370
the greater the damage will be.

318
00:40:35,954 --> 00:40:38,997
A new one.

319
00:40:39,081 --> 00:40:41,872
You've brought us the one.

320
00:40:55,420 --> 00:40:58,170
Interesting breeder.

321
00:41:14,218 --> 00:41:16,843
Making entry.

322
00:41:16,927 --> 00:41:20,680
- This won't take long.

323
00:41:20,763 --> 00:41:23,805
We've entered his neocortex.

324
00:41:23,888 --> 00:41:27,765
- Ahh! The Riddick!
- Regress.

325
00:41:27,848 --> 00:41:31,474
Scanning fresh memories.

326
00:41:31,557 --> 00:41:34,558
Thoughts of someone called Jack.

327
00:41:34,642 --> 00:41:36,558
Riddick!

328
00:41:38,393 --> 00:41:40,478
She went to prison.

329
00:41:41,602 --> 00:41:44,646
Now we find thoughts of an Elemental.

330
00:41:44,729 --> 00:41:47,896
The one race that would slow
the spread of Necromongers.

331
00:41:47,979 --> 00:41:50,232
- Furyans.
- Furyans.

332
00:41:55,566 --> 00:41:57,733
Where does he come from?

333
00:41:57,817 --> 00:42:02,319
Who are his people?
These are the things I need to know.

334
00:42:04,278 --> 00:42:07,196
We find energy.

335
00:42:08,530 --> 00:42:11,364
You must settle your past.

336
00:42:11,406 --> 00:42:16,408
We find Furyan energy.

337
00:42:16,449 --> 00:42:18,783
- For all of us.
- He's Furyan!

338
00:42:20,242 --> 00:42:22,325
Furyan!

339
00:42:23,993 --> 00:42:26,662
A Furyan survivor!

340
00:42:27,953 --> 00:42:33,664
Look at our world, at the graves of those
who didn't escape 30 years ago.

341
00:42:33,747 --> 00:42:36,207
There is no future
until we settle our past...

342
00:42:38,791 --> 00:42:41,875
for all of us
who bear the mark.

343
00:42:42,917 --> 00:42:45,710
Kill the Furyan! Kill the Riddick!

344
00:42:45,752 --> 00:42:48,752
Kill the Riddick! Kill the Riddick!
Kill the Riddick!

345
00:42:48,794 --> 00:42:51,003
Kill the Riddick!
Kill the Riddick.

346
00:43:25,266 --> 00:43:27,100
Who is this man?

347
00:43:28,975 --> 00:43:31,935
Find him. Whatever it takes. Find him!

348
00:44:06,739 --> 00:44:11,741
Let me guess.
A five-man crew this time.

349
00:44:11,825 --> 00:44:14,117
Couple of things
you could have done better.

350
00:44:18,452 --> 00:44:23,079
First, trash the locator beacon
inside my ship... the one you jacked.

351
00:44:23,162 --> 00:44:26,539
And second...and this is really
the more important part...

352
00:44:26,622 --> 00:44:29,831
dust my dick
when you get the chance.

353
00:44:29,914 --> 00:44:33,667
- Any questions?
- Yeah.

354
00:44:36,209 --> 00:44:37,834
What took you so long?

355
00:44:45,128 --> 00:44:47,379
Let's go, big boy.

356
00:45:00,050 --> 00:45:04,386
In and out, unsuspected and undetected.
Damn, I love a good smash-and-grab.

357
00:45:04,468 --> 00:45:07,012
Not so fast. Not so fast.

358
00:45:07,095 --> 00:45:09,513
Dickheads.
We're pickin' up fields here.

359
00:45:09,596 --> 00:45:12,556
Unknown fields detected on hull.

360
00:45:12,598 --> 00:45:16,140
I knew it. Here it comes.
This is some kind of scan.

361
00:45:16,223 --> 00:45:18,182
I don't know.
Readin' our Btus, maybe?

362
00:45:18,266 --> 00:45:21,766
- Let's drop one.
- Dropping.

363
00:45:29,812 --> 00:45:31,770
Decoy launched.

364
00:45:37,606 --> 00:45:40,566
Preparing to engage ion drive.
So,

365
00:45:40,649 --> 00:45:44,568
where do we drop
your merc-killin' ass?

366
00:45:44,609 --> 00:45:46,943
Who's gonna pay
the most for you now?

367
00:45:47,027 --> 00:45:50,737
- Butcher Bay?
- Butcher Bay.

368
00:45:50,818 --> 00:45:53,570
Ten minutes every other day
on the dog run.

369
00:45:53,653 --> 00:45:56,612
Protein waffles aren't bad.

370
00:45:56,696 --> 00:46:00,573
Hey, how 'bout Ursa Luna?
Nice little double-max prison.

371
00:46:00,655 --> 00:46:05,034
They keep a cell open for me...
just in case I drop in.

372
00:46:05,117 --> 00:46:07,034
You know the problem
with these joints now?

373
00:46:07,117 --> 00:46:10,077
Health clubs
for waffle-eatin' pussies.

374
00:46:10,161 --> 00:46:12,869
Maybe we should think about
uppin' our game here a little bit.

375
00:46:12,952 --> 00:46:15,329
Think about someplace
truly diabolical.

376
00:46:15,412 --> 00:46:17,371
What the hell is he thinkin' now?

377
00:46:17,455 --> 00:46:19,998
He's thinkin' a triple-max prison.

378
00:46:20,081 --> 00:46:23,415
A no-daylight slam.
Only three of 'em left in this system...

379
00:46:23,498 --> 00:46:27,832
two of 'em outta range
for a shitty little undercutter
like this one with no legs.

380
00:46:27,915 --> 00:46:31,417
Leavin' just... one...

381
00:46:31,500 --> 00:46:34,461
Crematoria.

382
00:46:34,502 --> 00:46:37,336
That is what you had in mind,
right, Toombs?

383
00:46:37,378 --> 00:46:41,004
- Hey, how does he know
where we're goin', and we don't?
- Dope it out.

384
00:46:41,087 --> 00:46:43,839
- I hate this run.
- Just do it!

385
00:46:43,922 --> 00:46:46,590
Don't know about this
new crew of yours.

386
00:46:46,673 --> 00:46:50,008
They seem a bit skittish.

387
00:46:50,091 --> 00:46:53,593
Probably shouldn't tell 'em
what happened to the last crew.

388
00:47:01,304 --> 00:47:05,805
You know, you supposed
to be some slick-shit killer.

389
00:47:05,889 --> 00:47:08,431
Now look at you...

390
00:47:08,514 --> 00:47:11,682
all back-of-the-bus
and shit.

391
00:47:48,237 --> 00:47:50,906
I say we attack Helion Two next.

392
00:47:50,988 --> 00:47:52,906
Take it straight
into their teeth.

393
00:47:52,989 --> 00:47:56,407
It'll cost you 20,000 heads,
five warrior ships.
Nothing more, I swear it.

394
00:47:56,449 --> 00:47:59,784
While I do prize brute force,

395
00:47:59,867 --> 00:48:02,993
this approach
is perhaps more artful.

396
00:48:03,076 --> 00:48:05,911
Start at the end.

397
00:48:05,994 --> 00:48:07,953
Go straight to Helion Five,

398
00:48:08,037 --> 00:48:10,246
the last planet
in the system.

399
00:48:10,330 --> 00:48:12,955
We approach from the night side.

400
00:48:13,039 --> 00:48:15,998
Remove these cannon first,

401
00:48:16,040 --> 00:48:18,873
then attack
the larger placements at speed.

402
00:48:18,956 --> 00:48:21,750
We'll catch them on their rear flank.
And in ten days?time,

403
00:48:21,833 --> 00:48:26,168
the rest of those worlds
will tumble before us.

404
00:48:26,251 --> 00:48:29,585
You see, as with most,
their blind spot...

405
00:48:30,427 --> 00:48:32,720
is right behind them.

406
00:48:33,003 --> 00:48:36,589
I've located an ion trail
which leads off-world.

407
00:48:36,631 --> 00:48:39,340
Then you should be
off-world, Vaako.

408
00:48:39,423 --> 00:48:42,008
I've deployed a tracker team.
One of the best.

409
00:48:42,091 --> 00:48:45,842
Wherever Riddick has gone,
you lens him out and cleanse him.

410
00:48:46,843 --> 00:48:50,802
- You.
- You want me to take a frigate
for one breeder?

411
00:48:50,886 --> 00:48:52,928
Don't question it, Vaako!

412
00:48:54,844 --> 00:48:58,054
Take it on faith.

413
00:49:01,223 --> 00:49:04,640
He's always been unsettled around you...

414
00:49:04,681 --> 00:49:06,725
the Lord Marshal.

415
00:49:06,808 --> 00:49:09,683
Unsteady.

416
00:49:09,767 --> 00:49:13,435
Perhaps because he knows
he's half the warrior you are.

417
00:49:13,518 --> 00:49:16,562
Some say he's too artistic
for the job.

418
00:49:18,063 --> 00:49:20,688
I wouldn't be surprised
if someone promoted him soon...

419
00:49:20,772 --> 00:49:23,731
to full dead.

420
00:49:26,107 --> 00:49:28,067
Take care what you say.

421
00:49:28,108 --> 00:49:31,026
Should I say it softly?

422
00:49:31,109 --> 00:49:34,067
So it sounds more
like conspiracy?

423
00:49:34,108 --> 00:49:37,986
Oh, why is it that when anyone
breathes about the demise of him
on the throne...

424
00:49:38,028 --> 00:49:40,695
everyone assumes
a conspiracy?

425
00:49:42,404 --> 00:49:45,781
Why isn't that
just prudent planning?

426
00:49:45,864 --> 00:49:48,366
When he is ready,
he will name a successor.

427
00:49:48,449 --> 00:49:50,532
Who?

428
00:49:50,616 --> 00:49:54,867
Toal? Scales? The Purifier?

429
00:49:54,951 --> 00:49:57,285
None of them...

430
00:49:57,369 --> 00:50:00,119
with the strength,
the dignity,

431
00:50:00,203 --> 00:50:04,287
of Lord Vaako.

432
00:50:04,371 --> 00:50:06,622
You can keep what you kill.

433
00:50:06,664 --> 00:50:09,956
- Stop.
- That is the Necromonger way.

434
00:50:09,997 --> 00:50:13,582
I said... stop.

435
00:50:13,666 --> 00:50:17,000
His death will come in due time
and not a moment sooner.

436
00:50:17,084 --> 00:50:20,668
- Why?
- Because I serve him. We all serve him.
It's called fidelity.

437
00:50:20,751 --> 00:50:22,920
It's called stupidity.

438
00:50:32,006 --> 00:50:34,007
Well, finally some attention.

439
00:50:46,928 --> 00:50:50,804
You have such greatness in you.

440
00:50:50,887 --> 00:50:53,013
If only you could see it like I do.

441
00:50:55,889 --> 00:50:57,890
You know what I want?

442
00:50:59,558 --> 00:51:03,559
Today I came up behind him
in perfect silence and he knew.

443
00:51:03,643 --> 00:51:06,102
I wanna go down
in Necropolis.

444
00:51:07,977 --> 00:51:09,977
Right now.

445
00:51:10,061 --> 00:51:15,105
His half-dead soul sensed I was
behind him. He sees everything.

446
00:51:15,188 --> 00:51:17,356
When no one is looking...

447
00:51:17,439 --> 00:51:19,982
when no one's around...

448
00:51:20,066 --> 00:51:22,357
I'm gonna get down on my knees...

449
00:51:24,067 --> 00:51:27,526
while you sit on the throne.

450
00:51:49,743 --> 00:51:53,578
- How unexpected.
- An Elemental.

451
00:51:53,662 --> 00:51:57,246
Here.
One of the captives.

452
00:51:57,329 --> 00:52:00,247
And why, after 30 years,

453
00:52:00,330 --> 00:52:02,580
should it be you?

454
00:52:02,622 --> 00:52:05,040
He doesn't regard her
as a captive, though.

455
00:52:05,082 --> 00:52:07,916
Elementals...
they talk of neutrality,

456
00:52:07,958 --> 00:52:09,959
but they're all witches
and spies.

457
00:52:10,042 --> 00:52:12,960
Why else would they
come and go like the wind?

458
00:52:13,043 --> 00:52:17,086
But where has he gone?
Where is the Furyan hiding now?

459
00:52:17,169 --> 00:52:20,088
You be the good warrior.

460
00:52:20,171 --> 00:52:23,047
Go after this Riddick.

461
00:52:23,131 --> 00:52:26,756
I'll find out why the Lord Marshal
is so threatened by him.

462
00:53:26,070 --> 00:53:30,029
Do you know
you grind your teeth at night?

463
00:53:31,823 --> 00:53:33,531
Sexy.

464
00:53:49,786 --> 00:53:51,800
Destination reached.

465
00:53:51,810 --> 00:53:53,900
Unlocking manual controls.

466
00:53:53,910 --> 00:53:57,664
All right. I make 700 degrees
on the day side,

467
00:53:57,706 --> 00:53:59,707
300 below on the night side.

468
00:53:59,748 --> 00:54:02,749
Let's not get caught in the sun.

469
00:54:02,791 --> 00:54:05,251
If I owned this place and hell,

470
00:54:05,293 --> 00:54:08,294
I'd rent this place out
and live in hell.

471
00:54:17,047 --> 00:54:19,464
- Blue angle... good.
- Stand by.

472
00:54:20,966 --> 00:54:22,966
And...

473
00:54:23,008 --> 00:54:24,967
Plotted course good.

474
00:54:25,009 --> 00:54:27,426
Hit it!

475
00:54:27,509 --> 00:54:31,343
Angle of approach, not good.

476
00:54:38,679 --> 00:54:41,389
- Look, Ma. No hands!

477
00:55:15,818 --> 00:55:17,777
Party poppers!

478
00:55:40,201 --> 00:55:42,578
I think I shit myself.

479
00:55:43,787 --> 00:55:46,955
Skittish, Toombs. Very skittish.

480
00:56:08,505 --> 00:56:10,422
Comfy?

481
00:56:27,887 --> 00:56:31,262
When the ride's over,

482
00:56:31,345 --> 00:56:33,889
your goggles are mine.

483
00:57:02,483 --> 00:57:05,524
Four-way split!

484
00:57:15,862 --> 00:57:18,155
29.4 kilometers.

485
00:57:26,658 --> 00:57:30,992
So, this is Riddick.

486
00:57:55,669 --> 00:57:59,712
What in the bowels of Christ
are you talkin' about, 700K?

487
00:57:59,795 --> 00:58:01,671
Don't take this one, boss.

488
00:58:01,755 --> 00:58:05,048
See? Anatoli here
has a nose for trouble.

489
00:58:05,131 --> 00:58:07,506
And this one, this Riddick guy...

490
00:58:07,547 --> 00:58:09,673
Big, big trouble.

491
00:58:09,715 --> 00:58:12,883
So, 700,000 is good money.

492
00:58:12,925 --> 00:58:16,717
I'd take the money, Toombs.

493
00:58:24,429 --> 00:58:28,931
The guild pays us a caretaker's fee
for each prisoner each year.

494
00:58:29,014 --> 00:58:33,058
We pay mercs 20% of that total fee
based on a certain life expectancy.

495
00:58:33,141 --> 00:58:34,767
How's about this?

496
00:58:34,850 --> 00:58:37,768
You open that safe you got hidden
behind the console there,

497
00:58:37,851 --> 00:58:41,977
show me the real books,
then we figure out my cut.

498
00:58:42,061 --> 00:58:44,019
Then I'll be on my way.

499
00:58:48,938 --> 00:58:52,272
Open my books.
This is what you suggest?

500
00:58:57,316 --> 00:58:59,317
Wasn't a suggestion.

501
00:59:17,200 --> 00:59:21,909
These are dangerous days,
if you believe the talk.

502
00:59:22,950 --> 00:59:25,952
Talk?
About dead planets.

503
00:59:26,035 --> 00:59:29,161
About some ghost army.

504
00:59:29,244 --> 00:59:31,913
About them.

505
00:59:31,996 --> 00:59:35,413
"Them"?

506
00:59:52,213 --> 00:59:54,129
I'll run the numbers again.

507
00:59:54,213 --> 00:59:56,297
It takes a couple of days,
probably,

508
00:59:56,381 --> 00:59:59,797
so you can stay as my guest.

509
00:59:59,838 --> 01:00:01,799
At least here, we are all safe.

510
01:00:01,840 --> 01:00:05,132
Yes?
Yes, boss.

511
01:00:05,216 --> 01:00:07,634
I'll give it a day.

512
01:00:09,967 --> 01:00:12,094
One.

513
01:00:50,566 --> 01:00:52,484
There are inmates...

514
01:00:52,567 --> 01:00:55,276
and there are convicts.

515
01:00:55,360 --> 01:00:58,819
A convict has a certain code.

516
01:00:58,902 --> 01:01:02,822
And he knows to show
a certain respect.

517
01:01:03,904 --> 01:01:06,447
An inmate, on the other hand,

518
01:01:06,489 --> 01:01:09,031
pulls the pin on his fellow man.

519
01:01:09,115 --> 01:01:11,532
Does the guards?work for them.

520
01:01:11,573 --> 01:01:14,157
Brings shame...

521
01:01:14,241 --> 01:01:16,617
to the game.

522
01:01:18,618 --> 01:01:21,577
So, which are you gonna be?

523
01:01:21,661 --> 01:01:24,203
Me?

524
01:01:26,287 --> 01:01:28,622
I'm just passin' through.

525
01:01:34,416 --> 01:01:36,583
Welcome to Crematoria.

526
01:01:42,752 --> 01:01:45,211
Should I go for the sweet spot?

527
01:01:45,253 --> 01:01:48,879
Left of the spine, fourth lumbar down,
the abdominal aorta.

528
01:01:48,963 --> 01:01:51,380
What a gusher.

529
01:01:53,714 --> 01:01:55,714
How do I get eyes like that?

530
01:01:55,756 --> 01:01:58,133
You gotta kill a few people.

531
01:01:58,216 --> 01:02:00,383
Did that.

532
01:02:00,466 --> 01:02:02,301
Did a lot of that.

533
01:02:03,885 --> 01:02:07,636
And then you gotta get sent to a slam.
One where they tell you you'll
never see daylight again?

534
01:02:07,719 --> 01:02:11,304
Only there wasn't any doctor here
who could shine my eyes,
not even for 20 menthol Kools.

535
01:02:11,388 --> 01:02:13,472
Was there anything
you said that was true?

536
01:02:16,265 --> 01:02:19,516
What are you gonna do, huh?
Go for the sweet spot?

537
01:02:19,558 --> 01:02:22,934
Remember who
you're talkin' to, Jack.

538
01:02:24,684 --> 01:02:28,018
Jack's dead.
She was weak.

539
01:02:29,186 --> 01:02:31,645
She couldn't cut it.

540
01:02:44,817 --> 01:02:46,984
The name's Kyra now.

541
01:02:47,025 --> 01:02:49,026
And I'm a new animal.

542
01:03:25,291 --> 01:03:29,959
They can be quite a test,
these deep runs...

543
01:03:31,792 --> 01:03:33,960
tests of our inner selves.

544
01:03:36,294 --> 01:03:38,669
Don't you find that true?

545
01:03:42,671 --> 01:03:44,672
Some men do.

546
01:03:46,089 --> 01:03:48,631
Just being so far from the armada,

547
01:03:48,715 --> 01:03:54,551
the mind can start to fill
with strange thoughts, doubts.

548
01:03:54,634 --> 01:03:57,594
Don't you ever have doubts, Vaako?

549
01:04:01,012 --> 01:04:03,512
- Doubts?
- About the campaign.

550
01:04:04,513 --> 01:04:06,680
About Lord Marshal.

551
01:04:08,681 --> 01:04:13,057
First and always,
I am a Necromonger commander.

552
01:04:14,142 --> 01:04:19,226
So if you're here to test my loyalty,
you succeed only in testing my patience.

553
01:04:19,310 --> 01:04:22,893
Oh, no.
No, that's not why I'm here at all.

554
01:04:44,319 --> 01:04:47,029
I'm so glad I could
steal you away for a moment.

555
01:04:47,112 --> 01:04:49,529
Doesn't it strike you odd?

556
01:04:49,571 --> 01:04:52,196
Here we have
the current Lord Marshal...

557
01:04:52,279 --> 01:04:56,365
destroying entire societies,
and yet he can't bring himself...

558
01:04:56,449 --> 01:05:00,408
to kill one
stranded Elemental.

559
01:05:00,491 --> 01:05:02,450
Why is that?

560
01:05:03,617 --> 01:05:05,577
You don't pray to our god.

561
01:05:05,618 --> 01:05:08,202
You pray to no god, I hear.

562
01:05:08,286 --> 01:05:11,246
Elementals... we calculate.

563
01:05:12,329 --> 01:05:14,288
Don't we all.

564
01:05:14,329 --> 01:05:18,248
But now let's have first things first.

565
01:05:18,331 --> 01:05:21,541
What of Riddick?
In truth, I don't know
where he went.

566
01:05:21,624 --> 01:05:24,542
In truth, I'm more interested
in where he came from.

567
01:05:26,710 --> 01:05:28,917
Watch your step.

568
01:05:29,001 --> 01:05:31,711
I've always wondered,

569
01:05:31,753 --> 01:05:34,378
does an air Elemental fly?

570
01:05:34,462 --> 01:05:36,421
Now do me a favor.

571
01:05:36,504 --> 01:05:40,465
Calculate the odds of you
getting off this planet alive...

572
01:05:40,548 --> 01:05:42,549
and now cut them in half.

573
01:05:44,007 --> 01:05:45,924
No, we can't fly.

574
01:05:46,008 --> 01:05:48,467
But we glide very well.

575
01:05:48,508 --> 01:05:51,343
Save your threats, Necromonger.

576
01:05:52,386 --> 01:05:55,970
I would have told you about Riddick
for the asking.

577
01:05:56,053 --> 01:05:59,847
It concerns a foretelling,
a prediction now more than 30 years old.

578
01:05:59,889 --> 01:06:04,223
A young warrior
once consulted a seer.

579
01:06:04,265 --> 01:06:09,349
He was told a child would be born
on the planet Furya...a male child...

580
01:06:09,433 --> 01:06:13,809
who would someday
cause the warrior's downfall.

581
01:06:13,893 --> 01:06:17,479
Cause his untimed death.

582
01:06:18,520 --> 01:06:23,481
Furya? Furya's a ruined world.
No life to speak of.

583
01:06:23,522 --> 01:06:25,105
For good reason.

584
01:06:25,189 --> 01:06:30,191
This young warrior
mounted an attack on Furya,

585
01:06:30,232 --> 01:06:33,359
killing all young males
he could find,

586
01:06:33,443 --> 01:06:37,527
even strangling some
with their birth cords.

587
01:06:37,611 --> 01:06:40,403
An artful stroke,
wouldn't you say?

588
01:06:42,320 --> 01:06:46,322
So this warrior, the one
who tried to outwit the prediction,
would later become...

589
01:06:46,405 --> 01:06:48,448
That's why he worries.

590
01:06:48,490 --> 01:06:50,490
The Lord Marshal.

591
01:06:52,115 --> 01:06:54,116
Which would make
the man-child...

592
01:06:54,200 --> 01:06:56,659
He worries he missed
killing that child in its crib.

593
01:06:56,701 --> 01:06:58,702
Riddick.

594
01:07:15,750 --> 01:07:17,918
That's why it's so vital to him.
Wait.

595
01:07:18,001 --> 01:07:20,375
- It's about a prophecy.
- Wait! Wait!

596
01:07:23,419 --> 01:07:25,419
Are you there?

597
01:07:28,962 --> 01:07:31,379
You do what your lord asks.

598
01:07:31,421 --> 01:07:35,089
You cleanse Riddick for him,
and in doing so...

599
01:07:35,173 --> 01:07:38,591
you prove your undying loyalty.

600
01:07:38,633 --> 01:07:44,260
And perhaps then
he'll finally let down his guard.

601
01:08:27,068 --> 01:08:28,610
Still here, I see?

602
01:08:28,693 --> 01:08:32,403
I've been here 18 years.
See this?

603
01:08:34,487 --> 01:08:40,322
I remember how gorgeous she was.
Well, gorgeous in a certain light.

604
01:08:40,405 --> 01:08:43,281
And now,
for the goddamn death of me,

605
01:08:43,365 --> 01:08:45,491
I cannot remember her name.

606
01:08:45,699 --> 01:08:48,158
Feeding time!

607
01:08:52,493 --> 01:08:56,495
We're here for the rest
of our unnatural lives.

608
01:09:04,539 --> 01:09:06,207
Here they come!

609
01:09:11,541 --> 01:09:15,418
Whatever you do,
don't make eye contact.

610
01:10:14,607 --> 01:10:16,066
Aaah!

611
01:11:41,222 --> 01:11:43,181
It's an animal thing.

612
01:11:54,142 --> 01:11:57,728
Check her for me.
She's always got a blade somewhere.

613
01:12:24,487 --> 01:12:27,781
Hyah!

614
01:12:57,499 --> 01:13:00,500
I don't think
she likes being touched.

615
01:13:02,668 --> 01:13:07,004
I'd take my wounded and go
while you still can.

616
01:13:12,463 --> 01:13:16,549
Is there a name for this
private little world of yours, huh?

617
01:13:16,591 --> 01:13:21,426
What happens there
when we don't just run away?

618
01:13:21,467 --> 01:13:23,969
You'll kill us... with a soup cup?

619
01:13:24,011 --> 01:13:26,344
Tea, actually.

620
01:13:26,428 --> 01:13:28,344
What's that?

621
01:13:30,928 --> 01:13:34,430
I'll kill you with my teacup.

622
01:13:46,184 --> 01:13:49,519
You know the rule. They aren't dead
if they're still on the books.

623
01:13:49,602 --> 01:13:52,729
Mmm.

624
01:14:10,193 --> 01:14:11,693
Come on.

625
01:14:34,578 --> 01:14:36,661
Death by teacup.

626
01:14:40,871 --> 01:14:43,288
Damn. Why didn't I think of that?

627
01:14:43,371 --> 01:14:46,205
I didn't come to play
"Who's the Better Killer?"

628
01:14:46,247 --> 01:14:49,666
But it's my favorite game.
Haven't you heard?

629
01:14:49,750 --> 01:14:52,167
I heard you came lookin' for me.
Is that all?

630
01:14:52,250 --> 01:14:54,918
Then you missed the good part.

631
01:14:54,960 --> 01:14:57,252
Hooked up with some mercs
outta Lupus Five.

632
01:14:57,294 --> 01:15:00,670
Said they'd take me on,
teach me the trade, give me a good cut.

633
01:15:01,962 --> 01:15:03,629
They slaved me out, Riddick.

634
01:15:03,671 --> 01:15:06,797
Do you know what that could do to you
when you're that age?

635
01:15:06,881 --> 01:15:10,466
When you're 12 years old?
I told you to stay in New Mecca.

636
01:15:10,549 --> 01:15:13,091
Did you not listen?

637
01:15:13,175 --> 01:15:15,342
I had mercs on my neck.

638
01:15:15,426 --> 01:15:17,884
I'll always have mercs on my neck.

639
01:15:17,925 --> 01:15:21,595
I spent five years on a frozen heap
just to keep 'em away from you.

640
01:15:22,594 --> 01:15:25,554
And you go and sign up
with the same fake badges...

641
01:15:25,596 --> 01:15:27,596
that wanted to cut you up
and use you for bait.

642
01:15:27,679 --> 01:15:32,055
What are you pitching, Riddick?
That you cuttin' out was a good thing?

643
01:15:32,139 --> 01:15:35,558
That you had my ass covered
from halfway across the universe?

644
01:15:35,641 --> 01:15:38,225
You signed with mercs.

645
01:15:41,977 --> 01:15:44,811
There was nobody else around.

646
01:15:57,690 --> 01:16:00,817
Let's pop the cork.
Get some fresh air.

647
01:16:37,914 --> 01:16:40,040
So they do go topside...

648
01:16:41,415 --> 01:16:44,208
to swap out air.

649
01:16:44,291 --> 01:16:46,709
Interesting.

650
01:16:46,792 --> 01:16:48,500
Who the hell are you?

651
01:16:50,461 --> 01:16:53,836
When it happens, it'll happen fast.

652
01:16:53,920 --> 01:16:57,339
Stay on my leg when I cut fence
or stay here...

653
01:16:57,422 --> 01:16:59,422
for the rest of your natural life.

654
01:16:59,505 --> 01:17:03,381
Nobody outs this place.
Nobody.

655
01:17:09,925 --> 01:17:12,260
He ain't "nobody."

656
01:17:26,306 --> 01:17:30,683
Good news first.
Talked things over with my amigos here.

657
01:17:30,725 --> 01:17:33,977
We'll cut you in for 775K.

658
01:17:36,394 --> 01:17:38,478
Well, all right.

659
01:17:38,562 --> 01:17:40,895
What's the bad news?
They close the local whorehouse?

660
01:17:43,605 --> 01:17:47,356
No. The bad news is worse than that.
Much worse.

661
01:17:47,439 --> 01:17:52,441
Our pilot, he saw this.
It crossed a shipping lane.

662
01:17:55,984 --> 01:17:59,486
Any idea what this might be?

663
01:18:03,112 --> 01:18:06,113
Never saw nothin' like it.

664
01:18:06,196 --> 01:18:09,864
This ship charts back
to Helion Prime.

665
01:18:09,947 --> 01:18:13,491
You know, Anatoli's
got a nose for trouble,

666
01:18:13,575 --> 01:18:17,617
and he thinks
trouble follows you here.

667
01:18:19,743 --> 01:18:24,078
Look. We dusted our tracks
and got the hell outta there.

668
01:18:24,162 --> 01:18:27,120
There is no way
we didn't lose them.

669
01:18:28,288 --> 01:18:31,164
"Them"?

670
01:18:36,623 --> 01:18:39,876
This is my prisoner. Mine.

671
01:18:39,917 --> 01:18:41,917
Nobody else's.

672
01:18:42,001 --> 01:18:44,335
And I want my money now.

673
01:18:44,419 --> 01:18:46,502
So...

674
01:18:46,586 --> 01:18:49,004
you stole a prisoner...

675
01:18:49,087 --> 01:18:51,088
from "them"?

676
01:19:58,321 --> 01:20:00,530
No.

677
01:20:00,614 --> 01:20:03,698
Riddick. No!

678
01:20:08,909 --> 01:20:12,908
Shoulda taken the money, Toombs.

679
01:21:08,888 --> 01:21:11,431
You gonna kill me?

680
01:21:44,777 --> 01:21:46,986
Mercs.

681
01:21:48,444 --> 01:21:50,904
Some guards here,
but this can't be all of them.

682
01:21:52,113 --> 01:21:55,447
Check their slots in the back...
and be careful.

683
01:21:55,489 --> 01:21:57,491
Don't bother.

684
01:21:57,574 --> 01:21:59,949
Guards ain't there.

685
01:22:00,033 --> 01:22:02,783
They figured out the Necros
are comin' for me.

686
01:22:02,824 --> 01:22:05,992
Plan was to clean the bank,
ghost the mercs,

687
01:22:06,076 --> 01:22:07,993
break wide through the tunnel.

688
01:22:08,077 --> 01:22:11,828
And then somebody got a lucky shot off
with this rocket launcher here...

689
01:22:11,870 --> 01:22:13,870
and took out the sled.

690
01:22:13,953 --> 01:22:18,081
Guards took off on foot
but rigged the door
so no one could follow.

691
01:22:19,164 --> 01:22:23,749
They'll take the one ship in the hangar
and leave everyone else here to die.

692
01:22:23,832 --> 01:22:27,209
How come you know all this shit?

693
01:22:27,292 --> 01:22:29,293
You weren't even here.

694
01:22:30,293 --> 01:22:32,419
'Cause it was my plan.

695
01:22:38,172 --> 01:22:40,713
I shoulda taken the money.

696
01:22:47,466 --> 01:22:49,716
Riddick!

697
01:23:00,304 --> 01:23:03,431
What is this?
What is he thinking?

698
01:23:03,473 --> 01:23:06,473
- Once that sun comes up...
- We'll last five minutes.

699
01:23:06,515 --> 01:23:10,475
Five minutes. We ain't gonna last
30 seconds out there.

700
01:23:10,558 --> 01:23:12,559
It'll light you up like a match.

701
01:23:17,143 --> 01:23:21,311
20-mile buffer zone
and 30 klicks to the hangar.

702
01:23:23,480 --> 01:23:26,730
30 klicks over that terrain?

703
01:23:39,277 --> 01:23:43,445
It's moving in the right direction.
We could make it.

704
01:23:43,820 --> 01:23:46,530
Stay behind the night,

705
01:23:46,571 --> 01:23:48,864
ahead of the sun.

706
01:23:48,948 --> 01:23:51,281
There's gonna be one speed...

707
01:23:54,406 --> 01:23:56,366
mine.

708
01:23:57,659 --> 01:23:59,826
If you can't keep up, don't step up.

709
01:23:59,910 --> 01:24:01,826
You'll just die.

710
01:25:05,976 --> 01:25:07,767
Riddick?

711
01:25:09,810 --> 01:25:11,810
Riddick?

712
01:25:15,187 --> 01:25:17,187
Riddick?

713
01:25:21,730 --> 01:25:25,233
Go, go! Go on! Go! Climb here!

714
01:25:25,316 --> 01:25:27,984
Climb! Go! Go, go, go!

715
01:25:53,701 --> 01:25:55,536
Boss!

716
01:25:59,370 --> 01:26:01,329
Up there.

717
01:26:01,413 --> 01:26:03,579
- Take a look.
- Because Anatoli says so?

718
01:26:03,663 --> 01:26:06,748
Because his nose says so.

719
01:26:24,045 --> 01:26:26,630
There's nothin' up here.

720
01:26:28,714 --> 01:26:30,131
Oh, shit.

721
01:26:39,926 --> 01:26:42,468
Riddick.

722
01:26:42,552 --> 01:26:46,179
They're heading
right for the volcano fields.
They're going for our ship!

723
01:26:46,263 --> 01:26:48,847
No chance do they
get to the hangar first.
No chance!

724
01:27:00,142 --> 01:27:02,351
Next one! Next hole!
We'll catch 'em there!

725
01:27:30,779 --> 01:27:33,072
No more run for you.

726
01:27:38,281 --> 01:27:41,740
Where did the big guy go?

727
01:27:47,493 --> 01:27:49,451
Ohh...

728
01:28:14,502 --> 01:28:16,253
Close it!

729
01:28:47,848 --> 01:28:50,682
What was that?
You don't care if you live or die?

730
01:28:50,265 --> 01:28:53,309
If I kill them first, not really.

731
01:28:54,934 --> 01:28:57,018
Maybe I do.

732
01:28:57,102 --> 01:28:59,103
Keep moving!

733
01:29:56,957 --> 01:30:00,043
Kyra?

734
01:30:00,126 --> 01:30:02,167
- Kyra!
- What?

735
01:30:02,208 --> 01:30:04,877
Get that ass moving!

736
01:30:42,599 --> 01:30:45,433
Riddick?

737
01:30:50,143 --> 01:30:54,103
Remember what I said
about not caring if I lived or died?

738
01:30:57,812 --> 01:30:59,980
You knew I was kidding, right?

739
01:31:03,273 --> 01:31:04,775
"One speed."

740
01:31:25,406 --> 01:31:27,281
Temperature differential.

741
01:31:27,364 --> 01:31:29,824
Your rope.

742
01:31:29,908 --> 01:31:32,283
It's too late.
We're never gonna make it.

743
01:31:32,366 --> 01:31:34,451
Your rope! Gimme your rope!

744
01:31:35,577 --> 01:31:37,660
And your water. All of it!

745
01:31:38,703 --> 01:31:42,162
Stay in the shadow of the mountain.
Don't wait for me. Run!

746
01:31:54,083 --> 01:31:56,459
Riddick!

747
01:32:07,505 --> 01:32:08,880
Aaah!

748
01:32:40,392 --> 01:32:42,352
Where the hell is that hangar?

749
01:32:47,354 --> 01:32:51,146
There it is.

750
01:32:53,146 --> 01:32:57,441
Listen.

751
01:33:22,783 --> 01:33:25,700
Let me guess. Necros.

752
01:33:25,784 --> 01:33:28,993
And a whole lotta Necro firepower.

753
01:33:29,035 --> 01:33:32,328
Shit! I hate not being the bad guys.

754
01:34:00,421 --> 01:34:05,548
I figure we got three minutes
before the sun hits us again,
burns out this whole valley.

755
01:34:05,632 --> 01:34:08,342
- Wait.
- We gonna do this or not?

756
01:34:08,384 --> 01:34:10,300
Just wait.

757
01:34:15,386 --> 01:34:17,553
Ellen.

758
01:34:18,970 --> 01:34:21,929
Her name was Ellen.
I never really forgot.

759
01:34:39,228 --> 01:34:41,853
Aaah! Boss!

760
01:34:53,108 --> 01:34:56,942
- Remember that favorite game of yours?
- "Who's the Better Killer?"

761
01:34:59,110 --> 01:35:03,111
- Let's play.
- Come on!

762
01:35:21,410 --> 01:35:23,077
On the right!

763
01:35:30,621 --> 01:35:32,413
Watch out!
Behind you!

764
01:35:32,496 --> 01:35:34,248
Kyra!

765
01:36:30,310 --> 01:36:32,352
Sybar!

766
01:37:33,916 --> 01:37:35,834
No!

767
01:37:57,884 --> 01:38:00,092
Aaah!

768
01:38:17,808 --> 01:38:20,517
Get up. Get up!

769
01:38:20,559 --> 01:38:22,560
Please get up.

770
01:38:35,857 --> 01:38:37,523
So,

771
01:38:38,940 --> 01:38:41,733
you can kneel.

772
01:38:59,198 --> 01:39:01,699
I think you know now.

773
01:39:03,366 --> 01:39:05,784
I think you know
who tore Furya apart.

774
01:39:09,160 --> 01:39:12,661
This mark carries the anger
of an entire race.

775
01:39:18,038 --> 01:39:20,122
But it's going to hurt.

776
01:41:38,007 --> 01:41:40,257
Kyra?

777
01:41:44,134 --> 01:41:47,051
I was supposed to
deliver a message to you...

778
01:41:49,011 --> 01:41:51,344
if Vaako failed to kill you.

779
01:41:53,220 --> 01:41:56,013
A message from
the Lord Marshal himself.

780
01:41:57,888 --> 01:42:01,390
He tells you to stay away from Helion,
stay away from him,

781
01:42:02,765 --> 01:42:04,891
and in return,
you'll be hunted no more.

782
01:42:11,852 --> 01:42:14,687
But Vaako will most likely
report you as dead.

783
01:42:16,104 --> 01:42:18,354
So this is your chance.

784
01:42:19,438 --> 01:42:23,188
Your chance to do
what no man has ever done.

785
01:42:23,272 --> 01:42:25,273
The girl.

786
01:42:25,274 --> 01:42:27,482
Where will they take her?

787
01:42:44,489 --> 01:42:47,824
We all began... as something else.

788
01:42:52,034 --> 01:42:56,659
I've done... unbelievable things...

789
01:42:57,660 --> 01:43:00,412
in the name of a faith
that was never my own.

790
01:43:02,328 --> 01:43:06,289
And he'll do to her
what he did to me.

791
01:43:12,541 --> 01:43:17,168
The Necromonger in me
warns you not to go back.

792
01:43:18,501 --> 01:43:21,128
But the Furyan in me...

793
01:43:24,713 --> 01:43:26,422
hopes you won't listen.

794
01:43:32,256 --> 01:43:36,925
God knows... I've dreamed of it.

795
01:44:38,156 --> 01:44:41,033
I have lost a Purifier...

796
01:44:42,283 --> 01:44:47,075
but I have gained
a first among commanders.

797
01:44:48,076 --> 01:44:50,702
It is overdue, isn't it...

798
01:44:50,785 --> 01:44:53,494
that we acknowledge
your many accomplishments,

799
01:44:53,536 --> 01:44:55,704
your steady faith,

800
01:44:55,787 --> 01:45:01,331
and above all,
your unflinching loyalty.

801
01:45:09,083 --> 01:45:12,544
Obedience without question.
Loyalty till UnderVerse come.

802
01:45:15,086 --> 01:45:17,087
Well done, Vaako.

803
01:45:18,338 --> 01:45:21,963
This is a day of days.

804
01:45:41,763 --> 01:45:44,263
Look more pleased, Vaako.

805
01:45:46,056 --> 01:45:49,474
You have killed his enemy...

806
01:45:49,515 --> 01:45:51,308
and his suspicions.

807
01:45:51,350 --> 01:45:56,143
- I should have brought back his head.
- You saw him unbreathing.
You saw him dead on the ground.

808
01:45:56,226 --> 01:45:59,227
Riddick was no common breeder.
In a heartbeat he dropped 20 of my men.

809
01:45:59,310 --> 01:46:03,270
All mysteries are not miracles,
not even in this religion.

810
01:46:05,771 --> 01:46:08,356
And if you say it is certain,
then it is certain,

811
01:46:08,439 --> 01:46:11,732
and we've already said it,
haven't we?

812
01:46:14,400 --> 01:46:16,400
We have.

813
01:46:20,151 --> 01:46:22,694
Now, tell me if it's true.

814
01:46:22,778 --> 01:46:26,987
Tell me the Furyan is gone,
and I can close this campaign
without hearing his bootsteps.

815
01:46:28,530 --> 01:46:30,489
If he is dead,

816
01:46:31,697 --> 01:46:33,699
I sense I'm not far
from the same fate,

817
01:46:34,782 --> 01:46:36,698
being of no further use here.

818
01:46:37,783 --> 01:46:40,867
Shouldn't I tell you
that Riddick is still alive?

819
01:46:40,909 --> 01:46:42,743
Don't try me, Aereon.

820
01:46:42,785 --> 01:46:45,077
I could plow you under
with the rest of Helion Prime.

821
01:46:45,118 --> 01:46:47,453
No one really knows the future.

822
01:46:47,536 --> 01:46:51,329
Then tell me the odds
that Vaako met with success,

823
01:46:51,412 --> 01:46:53,414
that I will now be the one...

824
01:46:53,498 --> 01:46:56,373
who can carry his people across
the threshold into UnderVerse,

825
01:46:56,456 --> 01:46:58,458
where they shall begin true life.

826
01:46:58,500 --> 01:47:00,833
Tell me what I want to hear, Aereon,

827
01:47:00,875 --> 01:47:05,002
and maybe
I'll save your home world... for last.

828
01:47:09,837 --> 01:47:12,337
- The odds are good...
- That?

829
01:47:12,420 --> 01:47:14,963
that you will reach the UnderVerse...

830
01:47:18,173 --> 01:47:20,174
soon.

831
01:47:58,562 --> 01:48:00,355
Ascension protocol!

832
01:48:00,438 --> 01:48:04,148
We still have numbers
out there, Lord Marshal...
sweep teams, recon ships.

833
01:48:04,190 --> 01:48:06,273
They would be hard-pressed
to make it back...

834
01:48:11,068 --> 01:48:14,902
Get my armada off the ground!

835
01:49:16,424 --> 01:49:20,009
- You mean on Helion?
- I mean here, on this very ship!

836
01:49:20,093 --> 01:49:24,386
Could you be wrong?
Mind fabricates fear.

837
01:49:24,469 --> 01:49:28,720
Could you be wrong?
Not so wrong as you
when you left him alive!

838
01:49:28,804 --> 01:49:30,722
It's twice a mistake.

839
01:49:30,805 --> 01:49:34,056
Not only your failure,
but now the report of success.

840
01:49:34,139 --> 01:49:37,724
How do we salvage this? How? How?

841
01:49:37,808 --> 01:49:40,350
Lord Marshal's got to be warned.

842
01:49:40,433 --> 01:49:42,393
You will never see the UnderVerse!

843
01:49:43,725 --> 01:49:45,851
He will kill us both
before our due time.

844
01:49:48,978 --> 01:49:50,937
I say give Riddick his chance.

845
01:49:55,772 --> 01:49:58,356
If he is half of what you think,

846
01:49:58,439 --> 01:50:00,440
he can at least wound the Lord Marshal...

847
01:50:00,524 --> 01:50:03,024
and that is when you must act.

848
01:50:03,108 --> 01:50:05,484
Just to take his place?
Just to keep what I kill?

849
01:50:05,526 --> 01:50:08,277
- That is the Necromonger way.
- It is not enough!

850
01:50:08,360 --> 01:50:11,112
Then you do it for the faith!

851
01:50:11,195 --> 01:50:13,904
If he has fear, he has weakness.

852
01:50:13,988 --> 01:50:15,904
If he has weakness, Vaako...

853
01:50:17,947 --> 01:50:20,114
He is unworthy of lordship.

854
01:50:21,115 --> 01:50:23,448
We do it for all Necromongers.

855
01:50:24,949 --> 01:50:27,118
Protect the faith.

856
01:50:27,201 --> 01:50:30,243
This can still be a day of days,

857
01:50:30,326 --> 01:50:32,411
but the timing...

858
01:50:32,494 --> 01:50:35,453
must be flawless.

859
01:50:57,295 --> 01:51:00,838
Final protocol.
Execute on my order.

860
01:51:35,767 --> 01:51:38,019
Go inside.

861
01:51:39,144 --> 01:51:41,144
Are they leaving now?

862
01:51:41,185 --> 01:51:43,979
Ziza! Go inside!

863
01:52:35,748 --> 01:52:37,999
We found this Lensor dead.

864
01:52:40,583 --> 01:52:44,042
Show me his last sight.

865
01:52:56,422 --> 01:52:58,131
Commander Toal.

866
01:52:58,214 --> 01:53:00,215
He won't escape twice.

867
01:54:52,631 --> 01:54:55,758
Stay your weapons!

868
01:54:57,216 --> 01:54:59,217
He came for me.

869
01:55:25,977 --> 01:55:28,353
Consider this:

870
01:55:33,229 --> 01:55:37,315
If you fall here now,

871
01:55:37,398 --> 01:55:39,315
you'll never rise.

872
01:55:39,398 --> 01:55:42,525
But if you choose another way...

873
01:55:43,692 --> 01:55:45,860
the Necromonger way...

874
01:55:45,943 --> 01:55:48,485
you'll die in due time...

875
01:55:48,526 --> 01:55:52,278
and rise again in the UnderVerse.

876
01:56:01,907 --> 01:56:04,115
Go to him.

877
01:56:11,661 --> 01:56:13,619
It hurts...

878
01:56:14,662 --> 01:56:16,913
at first.

879
01:56:16,996 --> 01:56:20,580
But after a while,
the pain goes away,
just as they promise.

880
01:56:22,997 --> 01:56:25,498
- Are you with me, Kyra?
- There's a moment...

881
01:56:25,581 --> 01:56:27,999
when you can almost
see the UnderVerse through his eyes.

882
01:56:29,333 --> 01:56:32,085
It makes it sound perfect...

883
01:56:32,168 --> 01:56:34,085
a place where anyone
can start over.

884
01:56:34,168 --> 01:56:36,628
Are you with me, Kyra?

885
01:56:49,174 --> 01:56:51,634
Convert now...

886
01:56:51,675 --> 01:56:53,843
or fall forever.

887
01:56:58,637 --> 01:57:00,886
You killed everything I know.

888
01:57:06,055 --> 01:57:07,222
Vaako.

889
01:57:09,348 --> 01:57:11,599
Not yet.

890
01:57:23,187 --> 01:57:26,146
Been a long time
since I've seen my own blood.

891
01:58:44,467 --> 01:58:47,426
These are his last moments.

892
01:59:07,058 --> 01:59:09,892
Give me your soul.

893
01:59:14,094 --> 01:59:17,512
Fuck you!

894
02:00:23,669 --> 02:00:25,920
You're not the one to bring me down.

895
02:00:44,927 --> 02:00:47,636
Now! Kill the beast
while he's wounded!

896
02:01:05,351 --> 02:01:08,352
Help me, Vaako. Kill him.

897
02:01:16,023 --> 02:01:17,357
Vaako?

898
02:01:22,025 --> 02:01:24,025
Forgive me.

899
02:01:24,108 --> 02:01:25,775
Flawless.

900
02:01:58,161 --> 02:02:00,662
No.

901
02:02:05,206 --> 02:02:08,625
No-o-o!

902
02:02:08,709 --> 02:02:11,792
Now what would be
the odds of that?

903
02:02:24,797 --> 02:02:27,382
I thought you were dead.

904
02:02:29,632 --> 02:02:32,175
Are you with me, Kyra?

905
02:02:34,258 --> 02:02:36,843
I was always with you.

906
02:02:39,178 --> 02:02:41,178
I was.

907
02:04:04,000 --> 02:04:07,209
You keep what you kill.


